  "summary": "Research & Development experience working in data communications in multi-threaded embedded real-time application development. Software development experienced in real-time embedded Linux and VxWorks -based systems for VoIP, wireless and various DSLAM communication products. As a member of Paradyne’s Technology Development Group, was involved in developing digital signal processing (DSP) algorithms for high-speed digital subscriber line (DSL) communication products. \n\n•Programming experience: Embedded C/C++, Linux Bash, TI DSP, TMS320C54x assembly, TI DSP TMS320C62x, Microsoft C/C++, PowerPC, ARM, MIPS, x86.\n\n•OS platforms: VxWorks, Linux, UNIX, Windows.\n\n•Development Tools: DDD, GDB, Tornado, TI Code Composer, Microsoft C/C++ development environment, Clearcase software management system.\n\n•VoIP /VoATM, DSLAM technology.\n\n•802.11 b/g/n wireless technology.\n\n•Digital Signal Processing:  communication algorithms, control systems, digital filters.\n\n•Mathematical Modeling Tools: Mathcad, Matlab, QED.\n\n•Hardware interfaces drivers for communication peripherals: SPI bus, DMA, RS232, Codec interfaces, ISA, PCI.\n\n•Hardware Experience: A/D, D/A, DSP-based Data Acquisition systems, Analog Circuitry, Modem Technologies, UART, FLASH.\n\n•Hardware Tools: oscilloscope, spectrum analyzer, vector signal analyzer, logic analyzer, emulators, packet analyzers, test instrumentation.",
