    "description": "Provided software design and development support for Paradyne’s 48-port Media Gateway and Broadband Loop Carrier equipment. Linux driver development for the SPI (Serial Peripheral Interface) host bus interface, hardware and software integration of the telephone subscriber line interface. Additional duties included Hardware Abstraction Layer (HAL) and Middleware software development under VxWorks and Linux. Supported customer field trials by troubleshooting and resolving software issues.  Coded and documented the user command line interface for various broadband communication cards\n\nLead DSP software developer for proprietary ReachDSL v2 broadband communication product. Hands on experience with various TI DSPs such as the TMS320C54x and TMS320C62x.  Collaborated on various DSP development tasks which included system software/hardware level design, modeling and simulation, DSP Development Tool selection and testing/integration of custom Analog Front End devices.",
